    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 7 USER]\ne057\tI am leaning toward accepting the slot, choosing a narrow theme about the family's first ten years in the neighborhood, and limiting the exhibition to material that Tomas and I both support displaying.\ne058\tWe would invite relatives to comment on draft captions and preserve disagreements where they matter, but not give everyone veto over the whole exhibition.\ne059\tI have not decided what “both support” means if Tomas thinks a disputed object is essential and I think the dispute itself makes it unsuitable.\ne060\tI also worry a one-month commitment will make that unresolved rule feel settled.\n[Turn 7 ASSISTANT]\ne061\tThe direction is narrower and more participatory, but the decision rule is still the heart of it.\ne062\tRequiring both of you to support every object protects the partnership and can also let one person quietly block the story.\ne063\tAllowing exceptions for “essential” material simply moves the disagreement into defining essential.\ne064\tYou may be able to commit to the slot while telling the center that final object selection depends on a process you have not completed.\ne065\tThat preserves the opportunity, though it also creates pressure and does not guarantee you and Tomas will reach a set you can both stand behind.",
