    "focal_turn_index": 7,
    "prior_context": {
      "alternative_citation_allowed": false,
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 6 USER]\ne047\tYes, he would hate an exhibition mainly about archival uncertainty.\ne048\tHe wants people to meet our relatives as people, not examples in a seminar about memory.\ne049\tI agree with him.\ne050\tI also learned that our mother would like to see something public while she can still participate actively.\ne051\tShe is not pressuring us, but that changes the cost of waiting for me.\ne052\tAt the same time, she tends to smooth conflict and may support captions that other relatives dispute.\n[Turn 6 ASSISTANT]\ne053\tYour mother's wish adds a meaningful time dimension without making speed automatically correct.\ne054\tHer participation could bring warmth and knowledge, while her preference for harmony is one perspective among several.\ne055\tThe exhibition might be designed around a limited period or theme where the evidence and permissions are stronger, leaving contested material in the archive for later work.\ne056\tBut selecting the least contested material could also produce exactly the smooth family story you are trying to avoid.",
